            "review_title": "Review at Ocean Club",
            "review_text": "Tasty Adventures\nChisinau, Moldova24 contributions\n0\nFrustration\nJan 2026 • Family\nWe're currently vacationing in Fukuoka with our husband and children. They saw the restaurant and decided to stop by spontaneously, as they had heard positive comments about it earlier.\n\nWe e-mailed about the reservation, but the responses were very slow, and in the end there was no clear confirmation whether or not there would be a reservation. Despite that, we decided to try our luck and arrived without confirmation.\n\nWe were greeted politely at the entrance, but were told that the table would be ready in about an hour and asked to wait in the lobby. We asked if we could spend this time in one of the hotel's bars or restaurants for a cocktail. For about 15 minutes, the employee insisted that we should wait in the lobby, which seemed strange and inhospitable.\n\nIn the end, we stuck to our point. As it turned out, the table was ready within 30 minutes, with the restaurant half-empty, and on the terrace, where we were also told everything was occupied, only one table out of four was actually occupied.\n\nAs for the cuisine - unfortunately, the food was completely mediocre and did not meet expectations or prices. It seems that the restaurant is overrated solely on the basis of the type and category of hotel, not the quality of the service and kitchen.\n\nExpected much more from an establishment of this level.\nRead more\nTranslated from Russian\nShow original\nWritten January 18, 2026",
